  "body": "main's ui lib is red: `diag::tests::shared_ui_code_prints_only_through_the_diag_seam` fails at upstream/main 9630c86e (Linux):\n\n```\npanicked at crates/ui/src/diag.rs:95:9:\nthese lines print directly, which a browser drops - use diag_warn!/diag_info!: [\"refusal_ghost.rs:44\"]\n```\n\n**Cause:** `crates/ui/src/refusal_ghost.rs:44` uses `eprintln!`. It came in with the refusal-ghost feature (90e3be04, #261 / PR #861). The diag-seam law (shared UI code prints only through `diag_warn!`/`diag_info!`, so the browser build keeps it) landed beside it. Each passed alone; together they're red.\n\n**Effect:** every PR's ui lib gate fails on this one test until it's fixed.\n\n**Fix:** replace the `eprintln!` with `diag_warn!` (or `diag_info!`), keeping the message.\n\nDone means: the ui lib is green at main; the diag-seam law holds.\n",
